# Intent: the library patch for the pinned private-network client (applied by scripts/fw-tailnet.sh to the downloaded copy outside this tree, never to the StackChan tree). (1) The net_io, derp_tx, derp_rx and coord task stacks live in PSRAM; wg_mgr keeps an internal stack because it writes flash and a PSRAM stack faults while the flash cache is off. (2) The fallback STUN host is the network operator's own relay host (port 3478), never a third party. (3) Port to ESP-IDF 6.1: component names (cjson, uart, gpio drivers), mbedtls 4 (no entropy or ctr_drbg objects, the WireGuard layer's own ChaCha20-Poly1305 for the Noise handshake with the byte order of the counter kept), lwIP without IPv6 (this unit builds lwIP with IPv6 off), and the stricter compiler.
# Placement: unit (library patch for the travel client; applied outside the unit tree)
# Upstream: components/microlink and its wireguard_lwip layer of the pinned client (MIT), see firmware/tailnet/PIN
# Check after a flash: the serial log shows the client's tasks start; self.tailnet.status reports internal_free at or above 25 KB while the client runs. The Noise handshake byte order is checked on a PC by host/tests/firmware/noise_aead_test.c against a standard ChaCha20-Poly1305 implementation.
